// expect: E0729, E0801
// Example 32 — Function-typed parameters (iter 51, BUGS.md BUG-022).
//
// `grammar/grammar.ebnf` line 88 gives the language function types:
// `function(String) returns Unit`. A call through such a parameter has
// no declaration to look up, so BOTH of Aether's boundary rules used to
// step over it silently:
//
//   * the marker rule (E0729) found no callee decl for `f`, so a
//     Secret<String> crossed into an unknown callee and every sink check
//     downstream went blind — `apply(print, pw)` logged the password;
//   * the effect rule (E0801) unioned only the CALLEE's effects, so a
//     `log` function handed to a `pure` helper by a `pure` caller
//     performed logging that nobody declared.
//
// Running this file prints ONE of the two. `aether check` reports the
// first non-empty analysis stage and stops (`transpiler/aether/passes/
// __init__.py`), and effects run before the security stage, so you see
// E0801 here. Give `main` and `apply` `effects log` and re-run: the
// E0729 below is what comes back. Both are in the `// expect:` header
// because `tests/test_corpus.py` reads every stage, not just the first.
//
// Both are refused now. There is deliberately NO sanctioned crossing at
// a function-typed parameter: a function TYPE's argument types are never
// checked against the function that actually arrives, and the grammar
// gives a function type no effects clause at all, so declaring one would
// be an exit that proves nothing. Unwrap at the call site instead, and
// declare the effect the passed value performs.

function logIt(msg: String) returns Unit
  effects log
do
  print(msg)
end

function apply(f: function(String) returns Unit, x: Secret<String>) returns Unit
  effects pure
do
  // E0729: `f` is a parameter — the analysis cannot see what it is.
  // `apply` can still claim `pure` while calling `f`: a function TYPE
  // carries no effects clause, so there is nothing here to check it
  // against. That residual is recorded in q1, not invented away.
  f(x)
end

function main(pw: Secret<String>) returns Unit
  effects pure
do
  // E0801: `logIt` runs under this call and it logs; main claims pure.
  apply(logIt, pw)
end
